'''Emil Pagliarulo''' is the senior design director at [[General:Bethesda|Bethesda Game Studios]], with credits on ''[[General:The Elder Scrolls|The Elder Scrolls]]'', ''[[General:Fallout|Fallout]]'', and ''[[General:Starfield|Starfield]]''.{{ref|name=MBG|[https://www.mobygames.com/developer/sheet/view/developerId,14020/ MobyGames] — ''Emil Pagliarulo''}}

Pagliarulo was a fan of ''The Elder Scrolls'' from the start, having played ''[[Arena:Arena|Arena]]'', ''[[Daggerfall:Daggerfall|Daggerfall]]'', and ''[[Redguard:Redguard|Redguard]]'' in the 1990s when they came out. He used to write articles and conduct interviews for Avault, one of which was for ''Redguard'', before he then moved on to work at [[Wikipedia:Eidos Interactive|Eidos Interactive]] on the ''[[Wikipedia:Thief (series)|Thief]]'' series. After being seduced by  emails from [[General:Todd Howard|Todd Howard]] about vibrant forests, Pagliarulo chose to join Bethesda Game Studios. 
