==Known Contributions==
This list is non-exhaustive and includes only contributions which have been confirmed to be implemented, fully or partially, by Pagliarulo.

*''[[Bloodmoon:Bloodmoon|Bloodmoon]]'' — Pagliarulo helped develop many of the side quests, including the encounter with [[Bloodmoon:Uncle Sweetshare|Uncle Sweetshare]].{{ref|name=25thPanel}}{{ref|name=RPGV|1=[https://web.archive.org/web/20050211154756/http://rpgvault.ign.com/articles/390/390344p3.html ''RPGVault: The Elder Scrolls III: Bloodmoon Interview'']}}
*''[[Oblivion:Oblivion|Oblivion]]'' — Pagliarulo authored the game's sneaking mechanics, the [[Oblivion:Dark Brotherhood|Dark Brotherhood]] questline and lore, as well as the [[Oblivion:Arena|Arena]] questline.{{ref|name=DevDiaryDB|[[General:Emil Pagliarulo: Now You See Me, Now You Don't|''Oblivion Developer Diary, Now You See Me, Now You Don't'']]}}{{ref|name=25thPanel}}{{ref|name=DBDoc|1=[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sqqVMVp39Xk ''Noclip: The Elder Scrolls IV: Oblivion - Designing The Dark Brotherhood'']}}
*''[[Oblivion:Knights of the Nine|Knights of the Nine]]'' — Pagliarulo wrote additional conversations.{{ref|name=KNC}}
*''[[Shivering:Shivering Isles|Shivering Isles]]'' — Pagliarulo provided voice acting for the male Dark Seducers.{{ref|name=OBVA|[[Oblivion:Voice_Actors#Shivering_Isles|Oblivion:Voice_Actors]]}}
*''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]'' — Pagliarulo was a senior designer and writer for ''Skyrim'', providing additional design support for the high level setting, factions, and cities featured in the game.{{ref|name=CitiesOfSkyrim|1=[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NQ7S2VA82Z4 ''Konsoll 2019: Emil Pagliarulo - Designing the Cities of Skyrim'']}} He authored the lyrics used in the game's main theme music, and a great deal of the Dragon Language and shout mechanics.{{ref|name=BehindTheWall|[[General:Behind the Wall: The Making of Skyrim|''Behind the Wall: The Making of Skyrim'']]}}{{ref|name=NoclipHistory}}{{ref|name=DragonLanguage|1=[https://bethesda.net/en/article/1rL4bCScN6RYXaXQb4ownj/how-bethesda-game-studios-made-skyrims-dragon-language ''Bethsoft: How Bethesda Game Studios made Skyrim’s Dragon language'']}} Additionally, the Dovahkiin's shouts both in the [[General:The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim - Official Trailer|game's trailer]] and in-game were voice acted by Pagliarulo.{{ref|name=DragonLanguage}}{{ref|name=TweetBGS|Bethesda Game Studios. (4 September 2021). [https://web.archive.org/web/20210904155021/https://twitter.com/BethesdaStudios/status/1434169387179728901 "Emil Pagliarulo (@Dezinuh) recording the original Skyrim shouts with Audio Director Mark Lampert and Todd Howard (photo credit). The all time epic VO session."]. Twitter.}} He designed the [[Skyrim:Dark Brotherhood|Dark Brotherhood]] questline, made design contributions to the [[Skyrim:Main Quest|Main Quest]], and designed the [[Skyrim:Blood on the Ice|Blood on the Ice]] side quest.{{ref|name=CitiesOfSkyrim}}{{ref|name=BehindTheWall}}{{ref|name=NoclipHistory}} The lockpicking minigame was also his design, a holdover from ''Fallout 3''.{{ref|name=NoclipHistory|1=[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QKn9yiLVlMM ''Noclip: The History of Bethesda Game Studios'']}} Pagliarulo also wrote the guard dialogue for the game, including the: "I used to be an adventurer like you. Then I took an arrow in the knee..." line.{{ref|name=NoclipHistory}} 
*''[[Skyrim:Dawnguard|Dawnguard]]'' — While Pagliarulo did not contribute to the add-on, he suggested the idea of the Prophecy of the Sun, with the earth forever becoming entombed in darkness.{{ref|name=BethPod|1=[https://web.archive.org/web/20131221100438/http://www.bethblog.com/podcast/ ''Bethesda Podcast #16'']}}
*''[[Online:Dark Brotherhood (DLC)|Dark Brotherhood]]'' — Pagliarulo provided feedback to the creators of the ''Dark Brotherhood'' DLC, informing them where they got certain things wrong and how the fiction the Dark Brotherhood should be designed.{{ref|name=25thPanel|1=[https://youtu.be/JITgbkbIJG4?feature=shared&t=745 ''Bethsoft: Bethesda Game Days – The Elder Scrolls 25th Anniversary Panel'']}}
*''[[SkyrimVSE:Skyrim Very Special Edition|Skyrim Very Special Edition]]'' — Pagliarulo wrote the dialogue for the game.{{ref|name=25thPanel}}

